# x86 Turn-2 collapse regression — locked state and fix path

Logline: Source-locked snapshot of the x86 backend regression introduced by the Turn-2 collapse on 2026-08-25/26, the C1 smoke measurement that proved it, the SSA _start: fix already in source, and the lane-respecting fixes queued for the next oodac rebuild.

Setup: Read-only audit. Source-locked evidence is the 50-fixture C1 smoke at ooda/scripts/x86_collapse_probe_smoke.oo (212 lines, double-run byte-identical). Pre-collapse v2 baseline is at audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot. All file paths are relative to /home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA.

Beats:
  1. State — what is on disk now, what regressed, what was fixed in source.
  2. C1 measurement — three passes: 0/50 → 0/50 → 16/50 COMPILED.
  3. Root cause — the SSA path emits 6 nops and (now-fixed) no _start: entry point.
  4. Lane map — what each agent owns; what is in my x86 lane; what is not.
  5. Fix path — four remaining moves, ordered by impact.
  6. Subsequent findings — the _start: refactor, label-safety lock smoke, opcodes 36-40 fix, cond_br je/jne fix, plus 3rd C1 measurement showing 16/50 COMPILED.

File: openOODA/audit/x86-collapse-regression.oot
Date: 2026-08-26 12:00
Status: open — third C1 measurement captured at 11:45 against the 11:45 oodac/oodac binary (which has my source commits up through 0462d2eb: contract-gate, sanitize_label, _start refactor, opcodes 36-40, cond_br je). COMPILED 0/50 → 16/50. ASM_FAIL 31/50 → 3/50. Empty-stdout 0%. 16 x86 commits in flight.

