## 10. Subsequent findings (after the original audit)

### 10.1 The `_start:` duplicate-symbol bug (commit 06b1d27a)

`x86_ssa_emit_function` hardcoded a `_start:` label inside every function body, so any program with > 1 function declared the same `_start:` symbol twice and `as`/`ld` rejected it. `test_x86_ssa_smoke.oo:3` explicitly exercises the multi-function case.

Fix: `x86_ssa_emit_function` is a thin shim that calls `x86_ssa_emit_function_impl(fn_data, 1)`. The if-branch (is_entry==1) emits `.globl _start` + `_start:`; the else-branch omits both. `x86_ssa_emit_program` calls the impl with `i == 0` as is_entry. Post-refactor the impl has exactly 1 `_start:` and 1 `.globl _start`. File at 218 lines, under 256 cap.

### 10.2 SSA label-safety lock smoke (commits 4b2a2e1c, 1a3613e1)

`ooda/scripts/x86_ssa_label_smoke.oo` (92 lines, lock smoke — no rebuild required) verifies the SSA-label defenses: the `_start:` refactor wiring, the `sanitize_label` filter ranges [a-zA-Z0-9_] + "fn" fallback, the call sites on `(fn_data).name` and `bname`, and (after 1a3613e1) the opcodes 36-40 handling + their acc-update list membership. Fails closed with `process_exit(1)`.

### 10.3 v0.220.0 oodac_bin empirical state (11:17 build)

The 11:17 oodac_bin was probed fixture-by-fixture. Result matrix:

| Fixture | Status | Opcodes |
|---|---|---|
| x86_int_add/sub/mul/div/rem | OK | 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 20, 23 |
| x86_int_gt/lt/gte/lte/neq | SEGFAULT | 38, 12, 39, 37, 40 |
| x86_fib | OK | 1, 20, 23, recursive |
| x86_float | OK | float ops |
| x86_match | SEGFAULT | match arms |
| x86_list | Runtime error | list ops |
| x86_struct | OK | struct ops |
| x86_call/alias/id_call/if_add | SEGFAULT | call, alias, if |

Pattern: the v0.220.0 binary segfaults on any SSA path that uses opcodes 36-40 (extended compare) or on call/alias/if/match. Consistent with `x86_ssa_format_inst` falling through to the `nop` else-branch (silent miscompile) and the resulting assembly being structurally broken.

Two distinct bugs in the v0.220.0 binary:
- **Name field truncation**: 11:09 build emits `.L^A^@^@^@_end:` (binary garbage), 11:17 build emits `.Lma_end:` (truncated to "ma"). `b53620ae` defense works (no garbage reaches `as`) but the LLVM lane's name field is still truncated. Owned by LLVM lane.
- **Missing opcodes 36-40**: `if 2 > 1` (opcode 38) was a silent miscompile in v0.218.0+. `d9ff2af1` adds explicit cases. The segfaults on gt/lt/gte/lte/neq should resolve to real cmp/setcc sequences. The segfaults on call/alias/if/match have different root causes (call lowering, struct handling, control flow) and are out of scope.
